From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dmitry Afonchenko <undermove1@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 14:21:11 +0400
Subject: [PATCH 93/94] Command bar finds open tabs and sites first; spaces
 keep their place; pinned tabs aren't Peeks
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- ⌘T/⌘L work like the omnibox, not the New Tab page's search box: a site
  from history can be the default, completed inline, instead of the
  search always coming first (Arc).
- An open tab whose site or a word of whose title starts with what was
  typed comes first, picked: Return switches to it.
- Each space keeps where its list was scrolled to; switching back no
  longer jumps (it scrolled to the active tab, from the other space's
  place).
- Peek only for what a page opened: a pinned tab or favorite clicked in
  the sidebar while a pinned tab of another site was shown opened as a
  Peek (Navigate() makes the active tab the opener).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SwxrQ2eLfJ2bv8cCoG2va1
